    },
    {
      "source": "GetPublicIP",
      "rva_or_symbol": "sub_100A1070 (RVA 0x000A1070)",
      "description": "Original queries api.country.is/?fields=location. Patched to return AL=1 with SSO '0.0.0.0'. Caller sub_100A13B0 stores string into global at unk_106BCFB8 for later reporting. Fixed value '0.0.0.0' is an obvious server-side pattern — every patched client emits identical sentinel IP. Server can filter/flag.",
      "severity": "med"
    },
    {
      "source": "SteamAPI_GetHSteamUser IAT",
      "rva_or_symbol": "IAT RVA 0x00546440",
      "description": "Both call sites rewritten to 'mov eax, <random>; nop'. The random value is odd (a2 | 1) and positive but random per patcher run. HSteamUser is an opaque token; downstream code treating it as ISteamUser* pointer would crash. In csgo_gc.dll it appears only used for identity comparison in reporting — safe as opaque ID. However, SteamAPI_RegisterCallback and SteamAPI_RunCallbacks are NOT patched — Steam callbacks still fire with genuine SteamID64 payloads that any csgo_gc code path can capture and send to gc.project446.su.",
