      "risk": "Challenge9205 (sub_1006F850) INTENTIONALLY left un-patched and still transmits msg 9205 protobuf to gc.project446.su via sub_100D88D0. It calls ScanEntry (patched → 0 findings) → builds a valid CMsgGCCStrike15_v2_ClientReportValidation with result_code=3 and sends it. Server-side, Project446 backend may compare our client's zero-finding pattern against expected native-VAC findings; a persistent 'zero on every re-validation' signature can itself become a heuristic detector. This is OUT-OF-DLL surface — no local mitigation possible.",
